<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Pathway xmlns="http://pathvisio.org/GPML/2021" title="β-alanine biosynthesis II" organism="cellular organisms" source="PlantCyc" version="20260304101735">
  <Xref identifier="PWY-3941" dataSource="MetaCyc" />
  <Description>&lt;i&gt;Supporting evidence for this pathway in Oryza sativa Japonica Group&lt;/i&gt;: This pathway is on the list of Ubiquitous Plant Pathways (UPP) that was generated for the COMET project, which includes pathways that are thought to be present in all or most land plants. All UPP pathways are automatically imported into databases regardless of Pathologic predictions. &lt;A href=&quot;https://www.plantcyc.org/about/savi-pipeline&quot;&gt;[more info]&lt;/A&gt; &lt;i&gt;Summary from MetaCyc:&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;General Background&lt;/b&gt; The existence of a biosynthetic pathway from |FRAME: PROPIONATE| leading to the formation of |FRAME: B-ALANINE| has been shown to exist in bacteria and plants |CITS:[stadtman55][13905315],[rathina02]|. In several plants, the synthesis of |FRAME: B-ALANINE| from |FRAME: PROPIONATE| has been shown by radiotracer ([&lt;sup&gt;14&lt;/sup&gt;C]-propionate) experiments |CITS:[13905315][rathina02]|. The exact intermediate steps of the biosynthesis are uncertain and almost no enzyme information is available for this pathway at the time of this review.</Description>
  <Authors>
    <Author name="PMN" />
    <Author name="xue" />
  </Authors>
